cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "The Gaussian-MMI synergy atom of integrated information decomposition is mostly self-prediction: code, record and results"
authors:
  - family-names: Sampalis
    given-names: Vasilis
    email: sampalisvasilis@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vasilis540/dmt-phiid"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, pre-specification record and results of a secondary analysis of DMT fMRI data with integrated
  information decomposition (Gaussian model, minimum-mutual-information redundancy): the sixteen atoms of two AR(1)
  processes with no lagged interaction in closed form, the DMT contrast, and a tool that puts each synergy value beside
  its AR(1)-substituted estimate (tools/ar1_diagnostic.py). The code is under the MIT licence; the text and result
  files outside manuscript/ are under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.md).
keywords:
  - integrated information decomposition
  - partial information decomposition
  - synergy
  - autocorrelation
  - fMRI
  - DMT
